Don't call `props.items.push(newItem)` -- props flow one-way from parent to child, and mutating the array in place changes the parent's underlying data through a reference the child was never supposed to write to, which Vue also warns about at runtime. Instead, declare a typed emit and let the parent decide how to update its own state:

```ts
const emit = defineEmits<{
  'add-item': [item: TodoItem]
}>()

function onAdd(newItem: TodoItem) {
  emit('add-item', newItem)
}
```

In the parent, listen for `@add-item` and push into its own `items` ref/reactive array there. Now the child never touches the prop directly, and the parent has one clear place where the list actually changes.
